// An acid lake crossed on crumbling stones, then an echo grown against a rock post, bent by it, its stone in the crook.
name Bent Echo
rule B1357/S1357
steps 3
hint The lake is crossed on stones that do not hold. Beyond it an echo grew against a post of rock and bent around it. The stone sits in the crook, against the post. The boulder before the echo is your step onto it.
tip An echo in the open is symmetric. This one is heavy on one side and empty on the other: the post blocked it. The stone is on the floor, right beside the post, on the heavy side.
intro A lake that eats lanterns, crossed on stones that fall. And past it an echo that grew crooked, because something stood in its way.
outro Bent, not broken. The post is still there. So is the shape.
say wake|The stones in the lake fall a heartbeat after you land. Do not admire the view.
say plant|Against the post. Growth leans away from what blocks it.
say grow|Three generations, one of them crooked.
say found|Crooked and exact. Up the echo.
say die|The lake does not give things back.
